{
  "_provenance": [
    "Captured live in DOSBox this session against PJOYG1.DAT (world 1, sublevel B).",
    "Three disjoint tick ranges, gaps disclosed rather than filled. Segment A",
    "(ticks 0,1,2,3,4,12,13,14,15,16,17,22,29,30 -- not contiguous, see the",
    "correction below for why) was rebuilt in a later pass of this same project;",
    "segment B (ticks 158-404) is the original clean run that watched DS:0x3bd",
    "clear on its own at cursor 405 -- exactly PJOYG1.DAT decompressed length --",
    "confirming a complete, correctly-terminated recording, untouched by this",
    "correction. Every other tick in 0-404 was never captured live -- in",
    "particular 5-11, 18-21 and 23-28 are NOT filled in: they would land in a",
    "proven-constant or linearly-bounded stretch and could be derived, but this",
    "project's own convention is a disjoint range with a gap, not asserted",
    "values a future diff could mistake for something independently read.",
    "Each sample is {tick, heroX, heroY, state, camX, camY}.",
    "Tick 0 (heroX=3424, heroY=608, camX=3296, camY=512) is independently",
    "confirmed by full disassembly of FUN_1000_8c34 (CS:0x8FBE-0x8FC3): reached",
    "from FUN_1000_006f's own init, gated by the one-shot DS:0x3e7 flag the joyg",
    "cycler dispatch sets, it is what actually writes DS:0x3bd:=1 and",
    "DS:0x282:=0 for joyg playback, hard-coding this exact hero/camera pair for",
    "DS:0x3e6==2 (joyg1).",
    "",
    "CORRECTION, later pass: the ORIGINAL segment A (ticks 0-18, contiguous)",
    "sampled DS:0x282, DS:0x17a/0x17c, DS:0x377 and DS:0xa/0xc at an unpinned",
    "point within each tick (a Lua wait_frames(1) poll, timed to whenever",
    "DS:0x282 was observed to have changed -- see replay-diff.mjs's own header",
    "for the full mechanism: a camera save/revert/restore dance at",
    "CS:0x023C-CS:0x02E4, and a state-machine write at CS:0x0254 that simply",
    "has not run yet if the poll lands early in the tick). Empirically this made",
    "ticks 0-2 correct (the poll happened to land past both events) and ticks",
    "3-18 each one recorded-input tick BEHIND where their own label claimed --",
    "confirmed by direct comparison against this pass's own live reads, which",
    "sample at CS:0x02F0 (after BOTH the camera final-restore and the",
    "state-machine write, on every tick) and tag each reading by DS:0x282",
    "itself rather than by poll timing. Because CS:0x02F0 supplies the LEAVING",
    "value of the tick that just ran (hero/state) and the ENTERING value of the",
    "NEXT tick (camera -- continuous, so leaving-T equals entering-T+1),",
    "building one honest tick=T record pairs the camera field from the",
    "cursor=T read with the hero/state fields from the cursor=T+1 read.",
    "This correction is also what exposed and let this pass FIX a real port",
    "bug: the original enters the TURN_LR/TURN_RL pivot (CS:0x5DFE) on ANY",
    "first press from ARRIVAL, not just a reversal -- ticks 14-15 (state 2",
    "then 1, hero frozen) were read by the OLD, wrongly-labelled capture as",
    "state 4 then 2, hiding the pivot entirely. Fixed in",
    "gods-web/src/game/player.js (_ground()); see that file's own citation",
    "for the disassembly this rests on.",
    "A SECOND divergence was found in this same pass and is NOW ALSO FIXED,",
    "in a later pass of this same project: ticks 29-30 (hero frozen at 3448",
    "on the tick RIGHT is first pressed again after the stop at tick 22,",
    "moving only from the NEXT tick) showed the original also delays one",
    "tick before resuming from a stopped WALK_R pose -- a different code",
    "path than the ARRIVAL fix above (stateIndex is already WALK_R, not",
    "ARRIVAL, when this delay happens). Root cause, confirmed by fresh",
    "disassembly of CS:0x5ACC-0x5AD3 (state 0) / CS:0x5D17-0x5D1E (state 1):",
    "the release path locks phase to a stopped-pose sentinel OUTSIDE the",
    "normal 0-7 walk cycle (CS:0x5B1E/0x5B26/0x5B2B/0x5B33, values 0x39/0x2d)",
    "-- confirming the untested candidate this file's own earlier revision",
    "named. On the resume tick the handler steps as usual, but the SAME",
    "clamp that caps a RAMPING phase at 7 sees the out-of-band sentinel and",
    "immediately UNDOES that step, pinning CL:=7 in place before the shared",
    "INC-CL/AND-CL,7 runs on it -- so the undo tick lands on phase 0, not 7;",
    "the tick after that (phase back in-cycle) steps normally. Fixed in",
    "gods-web/src/game/player.js (_ground()); see that file's own citation",
    "for the disassembly this rests on, and src/verify/checks.js for the",
    "phase-aware regression check this needed (X position alone cannot see",
    "a wrong post-clamp phase -- an earlier attempt at this exact fix got",
    "the phase wrong, 6 instead of 0, and only the phase check caught it)."
  ],
